      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Countries use sanctions because they are a primary, non-military instrument of foreign policy to achieve desired geopolitical outcomes. The moral argument for punishing human rights abuses is valid, but the reality is that sanctions are often selectively applied to serve strategic interests, not purely humanitarian ones. When they \"work,\" it is usually because the targeted regime is economically fragile or heavily reliant on international trade.",
      "source": "target",
